  "version": 1,
  "description": "Month starts of the Nanakshahi calendar as SGPC and Darbar Sahib print it. Each entry is the Gregorian date (IST) on which the month begins. A date belongs to the entry with the latest start on or before it, and the next entry's start ends it. The last entry only marks the end of the table.",
  "monthIndex": "0 = Chet ... 11 = Phagun. The year number changes on 1 Chet.",
  "sources": {
    "sgpc-archive": "SGPC Harmandir Sahib archive, POST https://hs.sgpc.net/hssearchhukmanamaTestCalender.php, selected_date=yyyy-MM-dd. The month start is the date minus (printed day - 1). Probed 2026-11-02.",
    "jantri-558": "SGPC Nanakshahi Jantri for NS 558 as listed in the nanakshahi-ical feed (MIT, janpreet/nanakshahi-ical). Dates in the future when probed.",
    "computed": "Sun enters each sidereal sign (Lahiri ayanamsa, Meeus solar longitude). The month starts on the Amritsar sunrise-to-sunrise day that contains that moment. This rule reproduces 107 of 109 month starts SGPC printed from 2017 to 2026, and both misses fall within 2 minutes of sunrise."
  },
